  "scope": "# Review handoff \u2014 a631936f7715\n\nTask/source: generator v1.8.0, SHA-256 `965a662deb1bad237758745f2b18ad53eda6f8d0bf3c8d3d4febaa74b1e18d30`, declared `RULE_HASH=8097fabedcc2`.\nDisposition: routine prototype follow-up completed; production generator and canonical Racket rule are unchanged.\nDefect \u2192 repair: setting-named public files and fixed 3-demo/1-query verification \u2192 exact visible-byte IDs, public/private separation, and independent demo/query controls.\nCurrent retained shape: 2 settings \u00d7 (3 demonstrations + 4 distinct queries) = 14 pairs.\nRacket evidence: both exact programs ran on every pair, 28/28 executions matched the Python mirror, and 8/8 queries were identifiable from demonstrations against the declared rival.\nFocused tests: 50/50 pass in `checks/task-tests-final/result.json`.\nAdversarial pass: 192 episodes, 1,344 pairs, 832 query checks across seeds 0..31 and count cases 1/1, 3/4, 4/8; no bounded finding.\nReference-rule changes: none. Prototype remains proposed/unapproved and exposes no production parameter API or training admission.\nRemaining limit: bounded sampling only through 4 demonstrations/8 queries; inherited exact-text authority formatting drift remains outside this prototype-only scope and was not rerun.\nNeeds attention: none for the repaired export/count contract; maintainers still own variant approval and the separate authority-formatting follow-up.",
